 "answer": "The `Prompt` object in promptfoo has a field called `label` that holds the text shown for the prompt in outputs and the web UI. This field is optional and can be used to provide a user-friendly display name for the prompt. If not specified, the `label` field can be populated by other means, as the `display` field is marked as deprecated. The relevant part of the TypeScript type definition from the context is:\n\n```typescript\ntype PromptConfigObject =\n  | {\n      id: string; // Path, usually prefixed with file://\n      label?: string; // How to display it in outputs and web UI\n      raw?: string; // Optional inline prompt text\n    }\n  | {\n      raw: string; // Inline prompt text\n      label: string; // How to display it in outputs and web UI\n      id?: string;\n      template?: string;\n      display?: string; // Deprecated: use label\n      function?: PromptFunction;\n      config?: any; // Provider config merged for this prompt\n    };\n```\n\nIn both variations of `PromptConfigObject`, the `label` field is designated for this purpose.",
